User types and their Functions
There will be three types of users with special rights, Doctor and Pharmacist.
Doctor:
Doctors can write prescriptions
Prescriptions are written based on each individual drug prescribed [Drug + Dose + Amount (for example: of pills)]
Doctors can view all patient records
Prescription Schema will be given by the professional (Ream).
Doctors can print the prescription on paper.
Doctor is assisted by autocomplete when typing in a drug. 
A drug list will be provided, the doctor cannot type anything. 
Pharmacist:
Can view prescriptions
Can not view private patient information. This is only for the Doctors to view.
Can give prescriptions
When a drug is given, the pharmacist inputs their Pharmacist ID for tracking, and inputs what part of the prescription they gave. This is important because if the pharmacist only gives part of the prescription, the missing prescription keeps it active until all drugs are given.
Admin:
Can view all registered accounts.
Can view all prescriptions given, can also view all the data related.
Can view in a limited manner the patient records. Can not however view the details. (We should later discuss this feature with the pharmacy professional)
Can send invite links to register a Doctor.
Can send invite links to register a Pharmacist.


